[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186133771 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-2cc2023e-80ab-5c70-bfaa-8494aaa05a23"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186134208 :question/problem "Let $u=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],v=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$ and $w=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$ be vectors such that $v$ and $w$ are orthogonal. Find $(u+9v)\\cdot w+v\\cdot (u+7w).$" :question/worked-solution "Since $v$ and $w$ are orthogonal vectors, we have that $v\\cdot w=0.$ Therefore, using linearity of the dot product to expand the parentheses, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u+9v)\\cdot w+v\\cdot (u+7w) & =u\\cdot w+(9v)\\cdot w+v\\cdot u+v\\cdot (7w) \\\\  & =u\\cdot w+9(v\\cdot w)+v\\cdot u+7(v\\cdot w) \\\\  & =u\\cdot w+9\\cdot 0+v\\cdot u+7\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =u\\cdot w+v\\cdot u \\\\  & =(4\\cdot 2+(-2)\\cdot (-5)+1\\cdot 7+(-3)\\cdot (-3)) \\\\  & +((-4)\\cdot 4+3\\cdot (-2)+5\\cdot 1+4\\cdot (-3)) \\\\  & =(8+10+7+9)+(-16-6+5-12) \\\\  & =34-29 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186131287 :answer-field/correct 17592186131292 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133770 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-a905591c-e962-54f6-a8cc-c6c8bf83d953" "question-fff3565b-721f-5145-afe3-b8fe4b216b1a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-a905591c-e962-54f6-a8cc-c6c8bf83d953" :question/id #uuid "a905591c-e962-54f6-a8cc-c6c8bf83d953" :question/math-academy-id "q-39987" :question/problem "If $u=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2k \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$ and $v=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}]$ are orthogonal vectors, then $k=$" :question/worked-solution "Since $u⊥v$, they are orthogonal vectors, we have that their dot product is equal to zero.\nFirst, let's calculate the dot product in terms of $k$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & ={u}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {v}_{4} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-5)+(-3)\\cdot 1+2k\\cdot 4+(-2)\\cdot k \\\\  & =-5-3+8k-2k \\\\  & =6k-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the dot product to zero, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6k-8 & =0 \\\\ 6k & =8 \\\\ k & =\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-3235cbb9-445e-59a3-8203-e82d292f2f8e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-3235cbb9-445e-59a3-8203-e82d292f2f8e" :answer-field/id #uuid "3235cbb9-445e-59a3-8203-e82d292f2f8e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-063cd8a4-7d99-5777-9168-56c532dfaca6" :answer-field/choices ["answer-bcbec869-0470-580f-b035-e097fc54e083" "answer-7397c384-842b-5369-95fb-1b1cd887ef97" "answer-0250a6fc-047f-5134-8219-025d2c93f557" "answer-63a57dbb-d4db-55f5-9f59-2754a4ca3e84" "answer-063cd8a4-7d99-5777-9168-56c532dfaca6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bcbec869-0470-580f-b035-e097fc54e083" :answer/id #uuid "bcbec869-0470-580f-b035-e097fc54e083" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7397c384-842b-5369-95fb-1b1cd887ef97" :answer/id #uuid "7397c384-842b-5369-95fb-1b1cd887ef97" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0250a6fc-047f-5134-8219-025d2c93f557" :answer/id #uuid "0250a6fc-047f-5134-8219-025d2c93f557" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-63a57dbb-d4db-55f5-9f59-2754a4ca3e84" :answer/id #uuid "63a57dbb-d4db-55f5-9f59-2754a4ca3e84" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-063cd8a4-7d99-5777-9168-56c532dfaca6" :answer/id #uuid "063cd8a4-7d99-5777-9168-56c532dfaca6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133772 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-308fc3e8-c583-59b4-999d-1160fdbc5784"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-308fc3e8-c583-59b4-999d-1160fdbc5784" :question/id #uuid "308fc3e8-c583-59b4-999d-1160fdbc5784" :question/math-academy-id "q-74190" :question/problem "Let $u=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ -1 \\\\ b \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],v=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],$ and $w=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$ be vectors such that $u$ is orthogonal to $v$ and $w.$ What is the value of $a-b?$" :question/worked-solution "Given that $u$ is orthogonal to $v$ and $w$, we have\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v=0 \\\\ u\\cdot w=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's consider the first equation $u\\cdot v=0.$ Calculating the dot product in terms of $a$ and $b$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & =0 \\\\ a\\cdot 2+(-1)\\cdot 4+b\\cdot (-2)+2\\cdot 5 & =0 \\\\ 2a-4-2b+10 & =0 \\\\ 2a-2b & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, for the second equation $u\\cdot w=0$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot w & =0 \\\\ a\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot (-3)+b\\cdot 1+2\\cdot (-3) & =0 \\\\ a+3+b-6 & =0 \\\\ a+b & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to find the values of $a$ and $b$, we need to solve the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2a-2b=-6 \\\\ a+b=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the second equation by $-2$ and adding the result to the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n-4b=-12\\,⟹\\,b=3.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $b=3$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2a-2(3) & =-6 \\\\ 2a-6 & =-6 \\\\ 2a & =0 \\\\ a & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have that\n\n$$\na-b=0-3=-3.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-c7504c88-811b-566a-be94-9e43fa618465"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-c7504c88-811b-566a-be94-9e43fa618465" :answer-field/id #uuid "c7504c88-811b-566a-be94-9e43fa618465" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-2e6d6850-cb8a-54f6-be70-b9a8c1c07ba7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4bdaf9a0-53ad-54b2-b4b6-e33f7f3ff1c7" "answer-2e6d6850-cb8a-54f6-be70-b9a8c1c07ba7" "answer-8f49ce40-633b-5445-b62b-5026574b4cc0" "answer-0f1be44e-4c09-570b-900c-d5331c4a7cb2" "answer-29d501de-e778-5839-9046-8064ae32b095"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4bdaf9a0-53ad-54b2-b4b6-e33f7f3ff1c7" :answer/id #uuid "4bdaf9a0-53ad-54b2-b4b6-e33f7f3ff1c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2e6d6850-cb8a-54f6-be70-b9a8c1c07ba7" :answer/id #uuid "2e6d6850-cb8a-54f6-be70-b9a8c1c07ba7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8f49ce40-633b-5445-b62b-5026574b4cc0" :answer/id #uuid "8f49ce40-633b-5445-b62b-5026574b4cc0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0f1be44e-4c09-570b-900c-d5331c4a7cb2" :answer/id #uuid "0f1be44e-4c09-570b-900c-d5331c4a7cb2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-29d501de-e778-5839-9046-8064ae32b095" :answer/id #uuid "29d501de-e778-5839-9046-8064ae32b095" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-fff3565b-721f-5145-afe3-b8fe4b216b1a" :question/id #uuid "fff3565b-721f-5145-afe3-b8fe4b216b1a" :question/math-academy-id "q-140124" :question/problem "Let $u=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ k \\\\ k \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$ and $v=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -k-1 \\\\ -7 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}]$ be vectors such that  $u⊥v.$ Find the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "Since $u$ and $v$ are orthogonal vectors, we have that their dot product is equal to zero.\nFirst, let's calculate the dot product in terms of $k$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & ={u}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {v}_{4} \\\\  & =7\\cdot 3+k\\cdot (-k-1)+k\\cdot (-7)+3\\cdot (-12) \\\\  & =21-{k}^{2}-k-7k-36 \\\\  & =-{k}^{2}-8k-15 \\\\  & =-({k}^{2}+8k+15)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the dot product to zero, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-({k}^{2}+8k+15) & =0 \\\\ -(k+5)(k+3) & =0 \\\\ k & =-5,-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-721d2419-eef5-5e91-a81c-c762d04fdf6d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-721d2419-eef5-5e91-a81c-c762d04fdf6d" :answer-field/id #uuid "721d2419-eef5-5e91-a81c-c762d04fdf6d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3ef489de-8397-5276-8e40-3eb47ebf67b7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5906b509-0f5b-5789-9f64-085720db0c8c" "answer-6e2302e0-f4bc-50ea-baa8-9ed96b988bd9" "answer-ae47675e-e182-568c-9d7f-237b8107f5d7" "answer-3ef489de-8397-5276-8e40-3eb47ebf67b7" "answer-bb0dcb46-938d-5272-bee5-f7421c4009e7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5906b509-0f5b-5789-9f64-085720db0c8c" :answer/id #uuid "5906b509-0f5b-5789-9f64-085720db0c8c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=-1,5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6e2302e0-f4bc-50ea-baa8-9ed96b988bd9" :answer/id #uuid "6e2302e0-f4bc-50ea-baa8-9ed96b988bd9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=-3,5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ae47675e-e182-568c-9d7f-237b8107f5d7" :answer/id #uuid "ae47675e-e182-568c-9d7f-237b8107f5d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=-5,-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3ef489de-8397-5276-8e40-3eb47ebf67b7" :answer/id #uuid "3ef489de-8397-5276-8e40-3eb47ebf67b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=-5,-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bb0dcb46-938d-5272-bee5-f7421c4009e7" :answer/id #uuid "bb0dcb46-938d-5272-bee5-f7421c4009e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=3,5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-2cc2023e-80ab-5c70-bfaa-8494aaa05a23" :question/id #uuid "2cc2023e-80ab-5c70-bfaa-8494aaa05a23" :question/math-academy-id "q-140126" :question/problem "Let $u=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],v=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ and $w=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$ be vectors such that $u\\,⊥\\,v.$ Find $(u-2v)\\cdot (v+2w).$" :question/worked-solution "Since $u$ and $v$ are orthogonal vectors, we have that $u\\cdot v=0.$ Therefore, using linearity of the dot product to expand the parentheses, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u-2v)\\cdot (v+2w) & =u\\cdot v-2(v\\cdot v)+2(u\\cdot w)-4(v\\cdot w) \\\\  & =0-2(v\\cdot v)+2(u\\cdot w)-4(v\\cdot w) \\\\  & =-2(3\\cdot 3+2\\cdot 2+(-2)\\cdot (-2)+2\\cdot 2) \\\\  & +2((-2)\\cdot 0+5\\cdot 2+7\\cdot 0+5\\cdot (-3)) \\\\  & -4(3\\cdot 0+2\\cdot 2+(-2)\\cdot 0+2\\cdot (-3)) \\\\  & =-2(21)+2(-5)-4(-2) \\\\  & =-42-10+8 \\\\  & =-44.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-798ee90a-3456-534c-b511-46a11430e83e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-798ee90a-3456-534c-b511-46a11430e83e" :answer-field/id #uuid "798ee90a-3456-534c-b511-46a11430e83e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-35773d41-e18d-5fce-a034-669f53d754f0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-f914dd17-6ae2-5347-bb6e-00d10036b162" "answer-d3ab5e73-3550-5ce2-810e-1d8800b0a15b" "answer-35773d41-e18d-5fce-a034-669f53d754f0" "answer-fab371f0-ea2c-5149-a335-661af52e0fef" "answer-b40f3ee7-6d48-5c77-8c17-7b2922b35b60"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f914dd17-6ae2-5347-bb6e-00d10036b162" :answer/id #uuid "f914dd17-6ae2-5347-bb6e-00d10036b162" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d3ab5e73-3550-5ce2-810e-1d8800b0a15b" :answer/id #uuid "d3ab5e73-3550-5ce2-810e-1d8800b0a15b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-36" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-35773d41-e18d-5fce-a034-669f53d754f0" :answer/id #uuid "35773d41-e18d-5fce-a034-669f53d754f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-44" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fab371f0-ea2c-5149-a335-661af52e0fef" :answer/id #uuid "fab371f0-ea2c-5149-a335-661af52e0fef" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "46" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b40f3ee7-6d48-5c77-8c17-7b2922b35b60" :answer/id #uuid "b40f3ee7-6d48-5c77-8c17-7b2922b35b60" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "50" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-6519472f-1465-50e9-8dc7-3b5144be25eb" :activity/id #uuid "6519472f-1465-50e9-8dc7-3b5144be25eb" :activity/title "Orthogonal Vectors in Euclidean Spaces" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049951 :activity/course 17592186046658 :activity/steps ["step-57427375-761d-5118-a063-f6c20e78f33a" "step-27b93922-d5e3-56f6-9165-297356e94309" "step-8593de49-4506-5427-a6da-5fafef9dd456" "step-b2bf8979-c070-5c18-8c76-af8d4e8cc4f8" "step-4d158392-5bc2-5a1a-99d8-29a76cb0bb41"] :activity/first-step "step-57427375-761d-5118-a063-f6c20e78f33a" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-57427375-761d-5118-a063-f6c20e78f33a" :step/id #uuid "57427375-761d-5118-a063-f6c20e78f33a" :step/content 17592186134208 :step/next "step-27b93922-d5e3-56f6-9165-297356e94309" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-27b93922-d5e3-56f6-9165-297356e94309" :step/id #uuid "27b93922-d5e3-56f6-9165-297356e94309" :step/content "question-a905591c-e962-54f6-a8cc-c6c8bf83d953" :step/next "step-8593de49-4506-5427-a6da-5fafef9dd456" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-8593de49-4506-5427-a6da-5fafef9dd456" :step/id #uuid "8593de49-4506-5427-a6da-5fafef9dd456" :step/content "question-308fc3e8-c583-59b4-999d-1160fdbc5784" :step/next "step-b2bf8979-c070-5c18-8c76-af8d4e8cc4f8" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-b2bf8979-c070-5c18-8c76-af8d4e8cc4f8" :step/id #uuid "b2bf8979-c070-5c18-8c76-af8d4e8cc4f8" :step/content "question-fff3565b-721f-5145-afe3-b8fe4b216b1a" :step/next "step-4d158392-5bc2-5a1a-99d8-29a76cb0bb41" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-4d158392-5bc2-5a1a-99d8-29a76cb0bb41" :step/id #uuid "4d158392-5bc2-5a1a-99d8-29a76cb0bb41" :step/content "question-2cc2023e-80ab-5c70-bfaa-8494aaa05a23" :db/ensure [:step/validate]}] "assertions" [[17592186134208 :question/problem "Let $u=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],v=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$ and $w=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$ be vectors such that $v$ and $w$ are orthogonal. Find $(u+9v)\\cdot w+v\\cdot (u+7w).$"] [17592186134208 :question/worked-solution "Since $v$ and $w$ are orthogonal vectors, we have that $v\\cdot w=0.$ Therefore, using linearity of the dot product to expand the parentheses, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u+9v)\\cdot w+v\\cdot (u+7w) & =u\\cdot w+(9v)\\cdot w+v\\cdot u+v\\cdot (7w) \\\\  & =u\\cdot w+9(v\\cdot w)+v\\cdot u+7(v\\cdot w) \\\\  & =u\\cdot w+9\\cdot 0+v\\cdot u+7\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =u\\cdot w+v\\cdot u \\\\  & =(4\\cdot 2+(-2)\\cdot (-5)+1\\cdot 7+(-3)\\cdot (-3)) \\\\  & +((-4)\\cdot 4+3\\cdot (-2)+5\\cdot 1+4\\cdot (-3)) \\\\  & =(8+10+7+9)+(-16-6+5-12) \\\\  & =34-29 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186134208 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] [17592186131287 :answer-field/correct 17592186131292] ["question-a905591c-e962-54f6-a8cc-c6c8bf83d953" :question/id #uuid "a905591c-e962-54f6-a8cc-c6c8bf83d953"] ["question-a905591c-e962-54f6-a8cc-c6c8bf83d953" :question/math-academy-id "q-39987"] ["question-a905591c-e962-54f6-a8cc-c6c8bf83d953" :question/problem "If $u=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2k \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$ and $v=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}]$ are orthogonal vectors, then $k=$"] ["question-a905591c-e962-54f6-a8cc-c6c8bf83d953" :question/worked-solution "Since $u⊥v$, they are orthogonal vectors, we have that their dot product is equal to zero.\nFirst, let's calculate the dot product in terms of $k$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & ={u}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {v}_{4} \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-5)+(-3)\\cdot 1+2k\\cdot 4+(-2)\\cdot k \\\\  & =-5-3+8k-2k \\\\  & =6k-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the dot product to zero, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6k-8 & =0 \\\\ 6k & =8 \\\\ k & =\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-a905591c-e962-54f6-a8cc-c6c8bf83d953" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-3235cbb9-445e-59a3-8203-e82d292f2f8e" :answer-field/id #uuid "3235cbb9-445e-59a3-8203-e82d292f2f8e"] ["answer-bcbec869-0470-580f-b035-e097fc54e083" :answer/id #uuid "bcbec869-0470-580f-b035-e097fc54e083"] ["answer-bcbec869-0470-580f-b035-e097fc54e083" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-bcbec869-0470-580f-b035-e097fc54e083" :answer/value "-4"] ["answer-7397c384-842b-5369-95fb-1b1cd887ef97" :answer/id #uuid "7397c384-842b-5369-95fb-1b1cd887ef97"] ["answer-7397c384-842b-5369-95fb-1b1cd887ef97" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-7397c384-842b-5369-95fb-1b1cd887ef97" :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}"] ["answer-0250a6fc-047f-5134-8219-025d2c93f557" :answer/id #uuid "0250a6fc-047f-5134-8219-025d2c93f557"] ["answer-0250a6fc-047f-5134-8219-025d2c93f557" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-0250a6fc-047f-5134-8219-025d2c93f557" :answer/value "1"] ["answer-63a57dbb-d4db-55f5-9f59-2754a4ca3e84" :answer/id #uuid "63a57dbb-d4db-55f5-9f59-2754a4ca3e84"] ["answer-63a57dbb-d4db-55f5-9f59-2754a4ca3e84" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-63a57dbb-d4db-55f5-9f59-2754a4ca3e84" :answer/value "5"] ["answer-063cd8a4-7d99-5777-9168-56c532dfaca6" :answer/id #uuid "063cd8a4-7d99-5777-9168-56c532dfaca6"] ["answer-063cd8a4-7d99-5777-9168-56c532dfaca6" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-063cd8a4-7d99-5777-9168-56c532dfaca6" :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}"] ["answer-field-3235cbb9-445e-59a3-8203-e82d292f2f8e" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-3235cbb9-445e-59a3-8203-e82d292f2f8e" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-3235cbb9-445e-59a3-8203-e82d292f2f8e" :answer-field/correct "answer-063cd8a4-7d99-5777-9168-56c532dfaca6"] ["answer-field-3235cbb9-445e-59a3-8203-e82d292f2f8e" :answer-field/choices "answer-bcbec869-0470-580f-b035-e097fc54e083"] ["answer-field-3235cbb9-445e-59a3-8203-e82d292f2f8e" :answer-field/choices "answer-7397c384-842b-5369-95fb-1b1cd887ef97"] ["answer-field-3235cbb9-445e-59a3-8203-e82d292f2f8e" :answer-field/choices "answer-0250a6fc-047f-5134-8219-025d2c93f557"] ["answer-field-3235cbb9-445e-59a3-8203-e82d292f2f8e" :answer-field/choices "answer-63a57dbb-d4db-55f5-9f59-2754a4ca3e84"] ["answer-field-3235cbb9-445e-59a3-8203-e82d292f2f8e" :answer-field/choices "answer-063cd8a4-7d99-5777-9168-56c532dfaca6"] ["question-a905591c-e962-54f6-a8cc-c6c8bf83d953" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-3235cbb9-445e-59a3-8203-e82d292f2f8e"] [17592186133770 :knowledge-point/questions "question-a905591c-e962-54f6-a8cc-c6c8bf83d953"] ["question-308fc3e8-c583-59b4-999d-1160fdbc5784" :question/id #uuid "308fc3e8-c583-59b4-999d-1160fdbc5784"] ["question-308fc3e8-c583-59b4-999d-1160fdbc5784" :question/math-academy-id "q-74190"] ["question-308fc3e8-c583-59b4-999d-1160fdbc5784" :question/problem "Let $u=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ -1 \\\\ b \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],v=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],$ and $w=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$ be vectors such that $u$ is orthogonal to $v$ and $w.$ What is the value of $a-b?$"] ["question-308fc3e8-c583-59b4-999d-1160fdbc5784" :question/worked-solution "Given that $u$ is orthogonal to $v$ and $w$, we have\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v=0 \\\\ u\\cdot w=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's consider the first equation $u\\cdot v=0.$ Calculating the dot product in terms of $a$ and $b$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & =0 \\\\ a\\cdot 2+(-1)\\cdot 4+b\\cdot (-2)+2\\cdot 5 & =0 \\\\ 2a-4-2b+10 & =0 \\\\ 2a-2b & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, for the second equation $u\\cdot w=0$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot w & =0 \\\\ a\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot (-3)+b\\cdot 1+2\\cdot (-3) & =0 \\\\ a+3+b-6 & =0 \\\\ a+b & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to find the values of $a$ and $b$, we need to solve the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2a-2b=-6 \\\\ a+b=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the second equation by $-2$ and adding the result to the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n-4b=-12\\,⟹\\,b=3.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $b=3$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2a-2(3) & =-6 \\\\ 2a-6 & =-6 \\\\ 2a & =0 \\\\ a & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have that\n\n$$\na-b=0-3=-3.\n$$"] ["question-308fc3e8-c583-59b4-999d-1160fdbc5784" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] ["answer-field-c7504c88-811b-566a-be94-9e43fa618465" :answer-field/id #uuid "c7504c88-811b-566a-be94-9e43fa618465"] ["answer-4bdaf9a0-53ad-54b2-b4b6-e33f7f3ff1c7" :answer/id #uuid "4bdaf9a0-53ad-54b2-b4b6-e33f7f3ff1c7"] ["answer-4bdaf9a0-53ad-54b2-b4b6-e33f7f3ff1c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-4bdaf9a0-53ad-54b2-b4b6-e33f7f3ff1c7" :answer/value "-2"] ["answer-2e6d6850-cb8a-54f6-be70-b9a8c1c07ba7" :answer/id #uuid "2e6d6850-cb8a-54f6-be70-b9a8c1c07ba7"] ["answer-2e6d6850-cb8a-54f6-be70-b9a8c1c07ba7" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-2e6d6850-cb8a-54f6-be70-b9a8c1c07ba7" :answer/value "-3"] ["answer-8f49ce40-633b-5445-b62b-5026574b4cc0" :answer/id #uuid "8f49ce40-633b-5445-b62b-5026574b4cc0"] ["answer-8f49ce40-633b-5445-b62b-5026574b4cc0" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-8f49ce40-633b-5445-b62b-5026574b4cc0" :answer/value "0"] ["answer-0f1be44e-4c09-570b-900c-d5331c4a7cb2" :answer/id #uuid "0f1be44e-4c09-570b-900c-d5331c4a7cb2"] ["answer-0f1be44e-4c09-570b-900c-d5331c4a7cb2" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-0f1be44e-4c09-570b-900c-d5331c4a7cb2" :answer/value "4"] ["answer-29d501de-e778-5839-9046-8064ae32b095" :answer/id #uuid "29d501de-e778-5839-9046-8064ae32b095"] ["answer-29d501de-e778-5839-9046-8064ae32b095" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-29d501de-e778-5839-9046-8064ae32b095" :answer/value "5"] ["answer-field-c7504c88-811b-566a-be94-9e43fa618465" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-c7504c88-811b-566a-be94-9e43fa618465" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-c7504c88-811b-566a-be94-9e43fa618465" :answer-field/correct "answer-2e6d6850-cb8a-54f6-be70-b9a8c1c07ba7"] ["answer-field-c7504c88-811b-566a-be94-9e43fa618465" :answer-field/choices "answer-4bdaf9a0-53ad-54b2-b4b6-e33f7f3ff1c7"] ["answer-field-c7504c88-811b-566a-be94-9e43fa618465" :answer-field/choices "answer-2e6d6850-cb8a-54f6-be70-b9a8c1c07ba7"] ["answer-field-c7504c88-811b-566a-be94-9e43fa618465" :answer-field/choices "answer-8f49ce40-633b-5445-b62b-5026574b4cc0"] ["answer-field-c7504c88-811b-566a-be94-9e43fa618465" :answer-field/choices "answer-0f1be44e-4c09-570b-900c-d5331c4a7cb2"] ["answer-field-c7504c88-811b-566a-be94-9e43fa618465" :answer-field/choices "answer-29d501de-e778-5839-9046-8064ae32b095"] ["question-308fc3e8-c583-59b4-999d-1160fdbc5784" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-c7504c88-811b-566a-be94-9e43fa618465"] [17592186133772 :knowledge-point/questions "question-308fc3e8-c583-59b4-999d-1160fdbc5784"] ["question-fff3565b-721f-5145-afe3-b8fe4b216b1a" :question/id #uuid "fff3565b-721f-5145-afe3-b8fe4b216b1a"] ["question-fff3565b-721f-5145-afe3-b8fe4b216b1a" :question/math-academy-id "q-140124"] ["question-fff3565b-721f-5145-afe3-b8fe4b216b1a" :question/problem "Let $u=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ k \\\\ k \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$ and $v=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -k-1 \\\\ -7 \\\\ -12\\end{aligned}]$ be vectors such that  $u⊥v.$ Find the value of $k.$"] ["question-fff3565b-721f-5145-afe3-b8fe4b216b1a" :question/worked-solution "Since $u$ and $v$ are orthogonal vectors, we have that their dot product is equal to zero.\nFirst, let's calculate the dot product in terms of $k$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & ={u}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {v}_{4} \\\\  & =7\\cdot 3+k\\cdot (-k-1)+k\\cdot (-7)+3\\cdot (-12) \\\\  & =21-{k}^{2}-k-7k-36 \\\\  & =-{k}^{2}-8k-15 \\\\  & =-({k}^{2}+8k+15)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the dot product to zero, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-({k}^{2}+8k+15) & =0 \\\\ -(k+5)(k+3) & =0 \\\\ k & =-5,-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-fff3565b-721f-5145-afe3-b8fe4b216b1a" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-721d2419-eef5-5e91-a81c-c762d04fdf6d" :answer-field/id #uuid "721d2419-eef5-5e91-a81c-c762d04fdf6d"] ["answer-5906b509-0f5b-5789-9f64-085720db0c8c" :answer/id #uuid "5906b509-0f5b-5789-9f64-085720db0c8c"] ["answer-5906b509-0f5b-5789-9f64-085720db0c8c" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-5906b509-0f5b-5789-9f64-085720db0c8c" :answer/value "k=-1,5"] ["answer-6e2302e0-f4bc-50ea-baa8-9ed96b988bd9" :answer/id #uuid "6e2302e0-f4bc-50ea-baa8-9ed96b988bd9"] ["answer-6e2302e0-f4bc-50ea-baa8-9ed96b988bd9" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-6e2302e0-f4bc-50ea-baa8-9ed96b988bd9" :answer/value "k=-3,5"] ["answer-ae47675e-e182-568c-9d7f-237b8107f5d7" :answer/id #uuid "ae47675e-e182-568c-9d7f-237b8107f5d7"] ["answer-ae47675e-e182-568c-9d7f-237b8107f5d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-ae47675e-e182-568c-9d7f-237b8107f5d7" :answer/value "k=-5,-1"] ["answer-3ef489de-8397-5276-8e40-3eb47ebf67b7" :answer/id #uuid "3ef489de-8397-5276-8e40-3eb47ebf67b7"] ["answer-3ef489de-8397-5276-8e40-3eb47ebf67b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-3ef489de-8397-5276-8e40-3eb47ebf67b7" :answer/value "k=-5,-3"] ["answer-bb0dcb46-938d-5272-bee5-f7421c4009e7" :answer/id #uuid "bb0dcb46-938d-5272-bee5-f7421c4009e7"] ["answer-bb0dcb46-938d-5272-bee5-f7421c4009e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-bb0dcb46-938d-5272-bee5-f7421c4009e7" :answer/value "k=3,5"] ["answer-field-721d2419-eef5-5e91-a81c-c762d04fdf6d" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-721d2419-eef5-5e91-a81c-c762d04fdf6d" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-721d2419-eef5-5e91-a81c-c762d04fdf6d" :answer-field/correct "answer-3ef489de-8397-5276-8e40-3eb47ebf67b7"] ["answer-field-721d2419-eef5-5e91-a81c-c762d04fdf6d" :answer-field/choices "answer-5906b509-0f5b-5789-9f64-085720db0c8c"] ["answer-field-721d2419-eef5-5e91-a81c-c762d04fdf6d" :answer-field/choices "answer-6e2302e0-f4bc-50ea-baa8-9ed96b988bd9"] ["answer-field-721d2419-eef5-5e91-a81c-c762d04fdf6d" :answer-field/choices "answer-ae47675e-e182-568c-9d7f-237b8107f5d7"] ["answer-field-721d2419-eef5-5e91-a81c-c762d04fdf6d" :answer-field/choices "answer-3ef489de-8397-5276-8e40-3eb47ebf67b7"] ["answer-field-721d2419-eef5-5e91-a81c-c762d04fdf6d" :answer-field/choices "answer-bb0dcb46-938d-5272-bee5-f7421c4009e7"] ["question-fff3565b-721f-5145-afe3-b8fe4b216b1a" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-721d2419-eef5-5e91-a81c-c762d04fdf6d"] [17592186133770 :knowledge-point/questions "question-fff3565b-721f-5145-afe3-b8fe4b216b1a"] ["question-2cc2023e-80ab-5c70-bfaa-8494aaa05a23" :question/id #uuid "2cc2023e-80ab-5c70-bfaa-8494aaa05a23"] ["question-2cc2023e-80ab-5c70-bfaa-8494aaa05a23" :question/math-academy-id "q-140126"] ["question-2cc2023e-80ab-5c70-bfaa-8494aaa05a23" :question/problem "Let $u=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],v=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ and $w=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$ be vectors such that $u\\,⊥\\,v.$ Find $(u-2v)\\cdot (v+2w).$"] ["question-2cc2023e-80ab-5c70-bfaa-8494aaa05a23" :question/worked-solution "Since $u$ and $v$ are orthogonal vectors, we have that $u\\cdot v=0.$ Therefore, using linearity of the dot product to expand the parentheses, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u-2v)\\cdot (v+2w) & =u\\cdot v-2(v\\cdot v)+2(u\\cdot w)-4(v\\cdot w) \\\\  & =0-2(v\\cdot v)+2(u\\cdot w)-4(v\\cdot w) \\\\  & =-2(3\\cdot 3+2\\cdot 2+(-2)\\cdot (-2)+2\\cdot 2) \\\\  & +2((-2)\\cdot 0+5\\cdot 2+7\\cdot 0+5\\cdot (-3)) \\\\  & -4(3\\cdot 0+2\\cdot 2+(-2)\\cdot 0+2\\cdot (-3)) \\\\  & =-2(21)+2(-5)-4(-2) \\\\  & =-42-10+8 \\\\  & =-44.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-2cc2023e-80ab-5c70-bfaa-8494aaa05a23" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] ["answer-field-798ee90a-3456-534c-b511-46a11430e83e" :answer-field/id #uuid "798ee90a-3456-534c-b511-46a11430e83e"] ["answer-f914dd17-6ae2-5347-bb6e-00d10036b162" :answer/id #uuid "f914dd17-6ae2-5347-bb6e-00d10036b162"] ["answer-f914dd17-6ae2-5347-bb6e-00d10036b162" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-f914dd17-6ae2-5347-bb6e-00d10036b162" :answer/value "-24"] ["answer-d3ab5e73-3550-5ce2-810e-1d8800b0a15b" :answer/id #uuid "d3ab5e73-3550-5ce2-810e-1d8800b0a15b"] ["answer-d3ab5e73-3550-5ce2-810e-1d8800b0a15b" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-d3ab5e73-3550-5ce2-810e-1d8800b0a15b" :answer/value "-36"] ["answer-35773d41-e18d-5fce-a034-669f53d754f0" :answer/id #uuid "35773d41-e18d-5fce-a034-669f53d754f0"] ["answer-35773d41-e18d-5fce-a034-669f53d754f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-35773d41-e18d-5fce-a034-669f53d754f0" :answer/value "-44"] ["answer-fab371f0-ea2c-5149-a335-661af52e0fef" :answer/id #uuid "fab371f0-ea2c-5149-a335-661af52e0fef"] ["answer-fab371f0-ea2c-5149-a335-661af52e0fef" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-fab371f0-ea2c-5149-a335-661af52e0fef" :answer/value "46"] ["answer-b40f3ee7-6d48-5c77-8c17-7b2922b35b60" :answer/id #uuid "b40f3ee7-6d48-5c77-8c17-7b2922b35b60"] ["answer-b40f3ee7-6d48-5c77-8c17-7b2922b35b60" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-b40f3ee7-6d48-5c77-8c17-7b2922b35b60" :answer/value "50"] ["answer-field-798ee90a-3456-534c-b511-46a11430e83e" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-798ee90a-3456-534c-b511-46a11430e83e" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-798ee90a-